      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "indeclinable ( स्वरव्ययं—Amara. ) and has generally the sense",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "of the acc. or loc. It is compounded with certain nouns as,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "स्वर्ग, स्वर्णदी, स्वाराट् ( स्वर्+राट् ) &c. धृष्टः—impudent, shameless",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "( निर्लज्ज ). The fig. of speech is विभावना.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 11. नाम—Verily, forsooth; or ‘ may well be considered’.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "ग्राह—A shark. वितर्क—misgivings, doubts; अस्मिन्कृते इदं भविष्यति",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "न भविष्यतीति चेत्यादयः ऊहाः Rámarshi. धैर्यद्रुमध्वंसिनी—felling the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "tree of courage on its bank. Cf. infra. सिकतिलनदीतीरतरुभिः Sl. 49.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "आवर्त—an eddy, a whirlpool. तटी—the bank of a river. The",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "comp. should properly be तटीका; but it may be defended by the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "maxim समासान्तविधिरनित्यः. तस्याः पारगताः—those that have",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "crossed it ( the river ) i. e. have conquered desire.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 12. संसारोत्पन्नं चरितम्—The course of life in this world;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "incidents of worldly life. अनुपश्यामि—to expect something good",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "out of, to see in prospect; cf. न च श्रेयोऽनुपश्यामि Bhag. I. 31. विपाकः",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "—result. विमृशतः—to me when I reflect, when I take a right",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "view of the matter. See Ni. S'a. 89. चिरपरिगृहीताः—( 1 ) enjoyed",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "for a long time, or (2) enjoyed after a long time, as Rámarshi",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "takes it. The former is, however, preferable, as long enjoyment",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "is required to make a man attached to worldly pleasures which",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "is implied in the succeeding line. महान्तो जायन्ते—become big;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "assume large proportions; hence tempt men by their magnitude.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "व्यसनं दातुमिव—their object in assuming big proportions and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "tempting men away from Moksha being as it were to make",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "men unhappy. The more a man clings to pleasures the more",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "miserable he becomes; for he is always disappointed; cf. न जातु",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "कामः कामानामुपभोगेन शाम्यति । हविषा कृष्णवर्त्मेव भूय एवाभिवर्धते ॥ Manu",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 16,
          "text": "II. 94. Or व्यसन may mean calamity; the fondness for enjoy-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 17,
          "text": "ments throws them into the turmoil of embodied existence; see",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 18,
          "text": "com. and infra. Sl. 46. notes. विषयिणां–and not to विरागिणां who at",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 19,
          "text": "once renounce them and become happy.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 13. चिरतरमुषित्वापि—even after staying long. वियोगे—is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "here used in the sense of ‘the vanishing of pleasures,’ and is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "explained by the words व्रजन्तः स्वातंत्र्यात् below. स्वयम्—of one’s",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
